column2:
Thus their life has gone in vain; seeing their youth and thinking it permanent — death sitting on their shoulders laughs, O Krishna, Vishnu; they, deluded in mind, do not know it.
garudpurana:306:64	'My house will last a hundred years, my sons likewise a hundred years; I too will live a hundred years in happiness, and my wife is of good marks;
garudpurana:306:65	I have cows full of good milk and friends full of joy; I will give my son to a bride, and give my daughter in marriage;
garudpurana:306:66	I will give my daughter or wealth to the good; I will always give to the rich alone.' Seeing again and again those devoid of the unseen, the Lord Vasudeva always laughs.
garudpurana:306:67	'I will not listen to the story, lest my fortune be destroyed; I will never worship Hari, lest the destruction of my sons and the like come about.'
garudpurana:306:68	Hari, called Dishta (Destiny), is Vasudeva, the giver of fruit to all in due time. Seeing such foolish people, Aurva, devoted to Vasudeva alone, wept.

All women who do not know such [a husband] are always widows. The embodied husband, merely an instrumental cause, a soul subject to fate, devoid of devotion to Hari,
garudpurana:307:33	very foul, leaking through nine openings, foul-smelling and always contemptible — for such a husband, dear father, there is no purpose apart from Krishna.
garudpurana:307:34	Divine women, leaving their own husbands, always please him who dwells there; therefore they are always wives with living husbands, to be revered by the worlds; there is nothing to consider here.
garudpurana:307:35	If husbands are devotees of Hari, the birth of such women is fruitful; through the accumulated merit of many births their husbands become devotees of Hari.
garudpurana:307:36	Women whose husbands are not devotees of Hari should give up their own bodies entirely; if they give up their bodies rightly, remembering Hari in the form of Krishna as their husband,
garudpurana:307:37	then there are no faults such as suicide for women; this is the conclusion in scripture. Women whose husbands do not know Vishnu should never associate with them.
garudpurana:307:38	Through the accumulated merit of many births their husbands would become devotees of Vishnu. In the Kali age devotees of Vishnu are rare, and devotion to Hari is always rare;
garudpurana:307:39	Hari's story is rare in the world of mortals, initiation into Hari is rare, very rare; determination of the truth of Hari is rare, and meeting with Hari's servants is rare;
garudpurana:307:40	circumambulation of Murari is rare, and salutation too, in Kali; the protection of his devotees is rare, and giving food to good Vaishnavas is rare;
garudpurana:307:41	worship of Murari according to the Tantras is rare, and taking Vishnu's name is rare; honouring good Vaishnavas is rare, and speaking with good Vaishnavas is rare;
garudpurana:307:42	touching the shalagrama is rare, seeing good Vaishnavas is rare; touching a cow is rare in the world of mortals, good singing and a good teacher are rare;
garudpurana:307:43	good wives and good sons are rare, and the sight of Hari dwelling on Sheshachala; very rare is the sight of Ranganatha on the bank of the Kaveri, which is Vishnu's river.
garudpurana:307:44	Service of Varadaraja at the sacred field of Kanchi, and his sight, are very rare in the world; the sight of Rama's bridge is very rare, and capacity in the Madhva scripture is very rare.
garudpurana:307:45	The noble say that the sight of Vishnu dwelling on the bank of the Bhima is very rare, and of Vishnu on the bank of the Reva, and of Vishnu's foot at Gaya,
garudpurana:307:46	and likewise of Vishnu dwelling at Badari — very rare for those living in the world of mortals; ascetics at Shrinivasa's hermitage on Sheshachala are rare in the world of mortals;
garudpurana:307:47	and at the place called Prayaga, the constant sight of Madhava is rare for men.
garudpurana:307:48	So I never want a husband other than Krishna. Having said this to her father, she went toward Sheshachala.
